[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_2uyj3")
description = "The Lyrian Empire lies in the temperate regions of the known world, forming both its geographical and political centre.

Humans and elves make up most of its female population, while halflings account for the majority of its men. Political power rests primarily in the hands of elven nobles.

The Empire is an ancient realm, founded by tall-folk seeking protection from the wild-folk and beast-folk of the north and south. Even after its founding, it remained under constant threat and frequently struggled to defend its borders.

Over the last few centuries, however, the Empire has adopted a more pragmatic approach. It has made peace with many wild-folk tribes along its borders, granting them free passage and trading rights while respecting their traditions.

Despite presenting itself as enlightened and civilized, the Empire has never abolished slavery. Halflings have kept hu-cows and ponygirls for thousands of years, similar practices among allied wild-folk are tolerated, and the Empire regularly raids hostile wildlands to its north and south in search of male breeding slaves."
img = ExtResource("1_1p0ut")
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://bkxhc74auednr"
